      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When addressing potential challenges, be transparent yet competent in your response. Acknowledge the scrutiny but also present the positive aspects of the litigation. For example, \"The current litigation presents us with both challenges and opportunities. While we’re employing our resources to defend our data processing patent, this experience has been invaluable in strengthening our legal position and refining our patent portfolio. Our proactive approach includes extensive research and development, ensuring continuous innovation and compliance, which bolsters the robustness of our intellectual property assets.\" Emphasize your company's commitment to resolving legal matters amicably and efficiently, assuring them of your ability to maintain strong control over your IP. This shows that despite the litigation, you possess a well-established track record and an experienced team dedicated to safeguarding your company's interests and ensuring a stable future.",
